# =============================================================================
#  VisTest — .gitignore
#
#  This is the .gitignore of the TOOL's own repository, and it deliberately
#  ignores ALL of .vistest/. Baselines are page content: capture an internal
#  system and the PNG and the DOM snapshot next to it hold that system's data.
#  Nothing captured on a developer's machine belongs in a public repository.
#
#  In a project that USES VisTest the rule is the opposite: commit your
#  baselines, or CI has nothing to compare against and the first run will
#  silently create new ones from whatever state it finds, broken included.
#  There, add these lines to your own .gitignore instead:
#
#      !.vistest/baselines/
#      !.vistest/baselines/**
#
#  PNGs grow git fast, so baselines are better off in LFS:
#      git lfs install
#      git lfs track ".vistest/baselines/**/*.png"
#      git add .gitattributes
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Secrets — the important part. None of this may ever reach a remote.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vistest/secrets.env
.vistest/secrets.*
!.vistest/secrets.env.example
secrets.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Saved browser sessions: cookies and localStorage after login.
# Effectively live access to your environment.
.vistest/state/
*.storage_state.json
storage_state.json
auth.json
cookies.json

*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
credentials.json
service-account*.json
gcloud-*.json
*.kubeconfig
.aws/
.ssh/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  VisTest runtime data — everything under .vistest/ except the example file.
#
#  baselines/  screenshots and DOM snapshots of the pages you captured
#  external/   the same, for connected third-party test suites
#  doctor/     diagnostic reports; they contain the target URL
#  runs/       run artifacts, several MB of PNG per full-page diff
#  projects.yaml   registry of connected suites: absolute paths, suite names
#  *.db        run history and metrics, local to each machine
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vistest/*
!.vistest/secrets.env.example
# `.vistest/*` rather than `.vistest/`: git cannot re-include a file that
# lives inside an excluded directory, so the directory itself must stay
# visible for the exception above to work.

# Generated tests and page objects: they are produced from the pages you
# captured, so their selectors, texts and URLs come from a real site.
tests/pages/
tests/.vistest_codegen.json
.vistest_codegen.json

# CLI and benchmark output
bench_out/
vistest-diff/
vistest-report/
*.actual.png
diff_*.png
combined_*.png

# Local config overrides (everyone has their own environment addresses)
vistest.local.yaml
vistest.local.yml


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Private working material that must never be published: plans, reviews,
#  audits, customer-specific notes, captured data pulled out of the tree.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
_private/
_to_delete/
private/
scratch/
*.internal.md


